  <div class="identity-copy">
    <h1>Yichao Xu</h1>
    <p class="position">{{ translate("Computer Science PhD candidate") }}<br>{{ translate("Johns Hopkins University") }}<br><span class="position-detail">{{ translate("Advisor:") }} <a href="https://www.yinzhicao.org/">Yinzhi Cao</a></span></p>

  </div>
    <nav class="contacts" aria-label="{{ translate("Profile links") }}">
      <a href="{{ 'cv-zh.html' if locale == 'zh-Hans' else 'cv.html' }}"><img class="link-icon" src="assets/icons/file-earmark-text.svg" width="14" height="14" alt="" aria-hidden="true">{{ translate("CV") }}</a>
      <a href="mailto:yxu166@jhu.edu"><img class="link-icon" src="assets/icons/envelope.svg" width="14" height="14" alt="" aria-hidden="true">{{ translate("Email") }}</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/samhsu-dev"><img class="link-icon" src="assets/icons/github.svg" width="14" height="14" alt="" aria-hidden="true">GitHub</a>
      <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/yichaoxu-jhu/"><img class="link-icon" src="assets/icons/linkedin.svg" width="14" height="14" alt="" aria-hidden="true">LinkedIn</a>
      <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=I8e-vacAAAAJ&amp;hl=en" title="{{ translate("Google Scholar, all-time citation metrics") }}"><img class="link-icon" src="assets/icons/mortarboard.svg" width="14" height="14" alt="" aria-hidden="true">{{ translate("Scholar") }} <span class="scholar-counts">{{ data['total-cites'] }} {{ translate('citations') }} · {{ translate('h-index') }} {{ data['h-index'] }}</span></a>
    </nav>
  </div>
</div>
<section id="research" aria-labelledby="research-title">
  <h2 id="research-title">{{ translate("Research") }}</h2>
  <div class="research-direction">
    <h3><img class="direction-icon" src="assets/icons/diagram-3.svg" width="16" height="16" alt="" aria-hidden="true">{{ translate("Program analysis") }}</h3>
    <p>{{ translate("I study how automated analysis can uncover vulnerabilities hidden in complex software behavior.") }}</p>
    <ul class="research-progress">
      <li><strong>{{ translate("Earlier:") }}</strong> {{ translate("Addressed blind spots in analyzing dynamic language behavior, uncovering previously unknown vulnerabilities: 54 in 19 real-world PHP applications (CoBrA) and 242 in npm packages (FAST).") }}</li>
      <li><strong>{{ translate("Now:") }}</strong> {{ translate("Detect business-rule violations, such as accepting an underpaid order, by using agents to bring application context into security analysis.") }}</li>
      <li><strong>{{ translate("Next:") }}</strong> {{ translate("Find and validate business-logic vulnerabilities across languages and applications, including settings without source-code access.") }}</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="research-links"><a href="#cobra">CoBrA · ICSE 2026</a><a href="#fast">FAST · IEEE S&amp;P 2023</a><a href="#discovery">AnonVul · {{ translate("Preprint 2026") }}</a></p>
  </div>
  <div class="research-direction">
    <h3><img class="direction-icon" src="assets/icons/robot.svg" width="16" height="16" alt="" aria-hidden="true">{{ translate("Agentic security") }}</h3>
    <p>{{ translate("I also study security risks in AI systems that plan tasks and use tools.") }}</p>
    <ul class="research-progress">
      <li><strong>{{ translate("Related work:") }}</strong> {{ translate("Showed that prior dialogue changes assistance on identical cybersecurity requests, highlighting the need to evaluate safety boundaries across conversational contexts.") }}</li>
      <li><strong>{{ translate("Exploring:") }}</strong> {{ translate("How can context and multi-step actions cause agents to act beyond their assigned task?") }} {{ translate("How can such logic vulnerabilities be detected and prevented?") }}</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="research-links"><a href="#context">3R-Bench · {{ translate("Preprint 2026") }}</a></p>
  </div>
</section>
<section id="publications"><h2>{{ translate("Publications") }}</h2><article class="publication" id="cobra"><details class="work-details"><summary class="work-summary"><span class="entry-label"><span class="entry-marks"><img class="entry-icon" src="assets/icse-2026.png" width="18" height="18" alt="" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="entry-label-text">ICSE 2026</span></span><div class="work-heading"><h3 class="work-title">CoBrA: Context-, Branch-sensitive Static Analysis for Detecting Taint-style Vulnerabilities in PHP Web Applications</h3> <span class="work-actions"><a href="https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3744916.3773195" aria-label="{{ translate('Paper') }}: CoBrA: Context-, Branch-sensitive Static Analysis for Detecting Taint-style Vulnerabilities in PHP Web Applications"><img class="link-icon" src="assets/icons/journal-text.svg" width="14" height="14" alt="" aria-hidden="true">{{ translate("Paper") }}</a><a href="https://github.com/jhu-seclab-cobra" aria-label="{{ translate('Code') }}: CoBrA: Context-, Branch-sensitive Static Analysis for Detecting Taint-style Vulnerabilities in PHP Web Applications"><img class="link-icon" src="assets/icons/code-slash.svg" width="14" height="14" alt="" aria-hidden="true">{{ translate("Code") }}</a><a href="https://www.yinzhicao.org/COBRA/cobra.pdf" aria-label="{{ translate('PDF') }}: CoBrA: Context-, Branch-sensitive Static Analysis for Detecting Taint-style Vulnerabilities in PHP Web Applications"><img class="link-icon" src="assets/icons/file-earmark-pdf.svg" width="14" height="14" alt="" aria-hidden="true">PDF</a></span></div></summary><div class="work-body"><p class="pub-meta"><span>{{ translate("First author") }}</span></p><p class="pub-description">{{ translate("PHP applications can choose which functions to call at runtime, making vulnerabilities difficult to detect statically. I designed and built CoBrA to resolve these calls using their calling context and track unsafe input flows. It found 54 previously unknown vulnerabilities in 19 web applications.") }}</p><p class="pub-authors"><strong>Yichao Xu</strong>, Mingqing Kang, Neil Thimmaiah, Rigel Gjomemo, V. N. Venkatakrishnan, Yinzhi Cao</p><details class="demo-disclosure" id="cobra-demo-details">
      <summary>{{ translate("How CoBrA works") }} <span>{{ translate("Resolve dynamic calls, then check the data flow") }}</span></summary>
    <div class="cobra-demo">
      <div class="demo-toolbar">
        <span class="demo-toolbar-label"><img class="demo-logo" src="assets/cobra.png" width="40" height="40" alt="CoBrA">{{ translate("Which paths can this request take?") }}</span>
        <div class="context-options" role="group" aria-label="{{ translate("Choose a calling context") }}">
          <button type="button" data-context="feed" aria-pressed="true">{{ translate("Feed call") }}</button>
          <button type="button" data-context="admin" aria-pressed="false">{{ translate("Admin call") }}</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="phase-controls" role="group" aria-label="{{ translate("CoBrA analysis phases") }}">
        <button type="button" data-phase="0" aria-pressed="true"><span>{{ translate("Phase I") }}</span>{{ translate("Dependency generation") }}</button>
        <button type="button" data-phase="1" aria-pressed="false"><span>{{ translate("Phase II") }}</span>{{ translate("Call paths generation") }}</button>
        <button type="button" data-phase="2" aria-pressed="false"><span>{{ translate("Phase III") }}</span>{{ translate("Vulnerabilities detection") }}</button>
      </div>
      <div class="phase-takeaway"><h4 id="phase-heading"></h4><p id="cobra-result" aria-live="polite"></p></div>

      <div class="demo-panels">
        <div class="demo-code-panel"><p class="demo-code-label">PHP</p><pre class="demo-code" aria-label="{{ translate("Simplified PHP example") }}"><code id="cobra-code"></code></pre></div>
        <div class="demo-graph-panel">
          <p class="demo-graph-label" id="graph-label">{{ translate("Dependencies within controller") }}</p>
          <p class="target-label" id="target-label">$action . "_controller" → ?</p>
          <div class="call-graph" id="cobra-graph" role="img" aria-label="{{ translate("Analysis graph; the current phase and result are described in adjacent text.") }}"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="demo-nav"><button id="cobra-next" type="button">{{ translate("Next: Phase II →") }}</button></div>
      <details class="technical-details"><summary>{{ translate("Phase details: input, method and output") }}</summary>
      <dl class="phase-explanation"><dt>{{ translate("Input") }}</dt><dd id="phase-input"></dd><dt>{{ translate("Method") }}</dt><dd id="phase-method"></dd><dt>{{ translate("Output") }}</dt><dd id="phase-output"></dd></dl>
      </details>
<details class="technical-details"><summary>{{ translate("Full reduced PHP example") }}</summary><pre class="full-code"><code id="cobra-full-code"></code></pre></details>
</div>
<p class="demo-caption">{{ translate("Adapted from the") }} <a href="https://www.yinzhicao.org/COBRA/cobra.pdf">{{ translate("paper’s Emoncms example") }}</a>{{ translate("; parsing, database setup and the other engine’s body are omitted. Predefined analysis states; no PHP or CoBrA execution.") }}</p>
</details></div></details></article>
<article class="publication" id="fast"><details class="work-details"><summary class="work-summary"><span class="entry-label"><span class="entry-marks"><img class="entry-icon" src="assets/ieee-sp-2023.png" width="18" height="18" alt="" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="entry-label-text">IEEE S&amp;P 2023</span></span><div class="work-heading"><h3 class="work-title">Scaling JavaScript Abstract Interpretation to Detect and Exploit Node.js Taint-style Vulnerability</h3> <span class="work-actions"><a href="https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/10179352" aria-label="{{ translate('Paper') }}: Scaling JavaScript Abstract Interpretation to Detect and Exploit Node.js Taint-style Vulnerability"><img class="link-icon" src="assets/icons/journal-text.svg" width="14" height="14" alt="" aria-hidden="true">{{ translate("Paper") }}</a><a href="https://github.com/fast-sp-2023/fast" aria-label="{{ translate('Code') }}: Scaling JavaScript Abstract Interpretation to Detect and Exploit Node.js Taint-style Vulnerability"><img class="link-icon" src="assets/icons/code-slash.svg" width="14" height="14" alt="" aria-hidden="true">{{ translate("Code") }}</a><a href="https://www.yinzhicao.org/FAST/ODGen-FAST.pdf" aria-label="{{ translate('PDF') }}: Scaling JavaScript Abstract Interpretation to Detect and Exploit Node.js Taint-style Vulnerability"><img class="link-icon" src="assets/icons/file-earmark-pdf.svg" width="14" height="14" alt="" aria-hidden="true">PDF</a></span></div></summary><div class="work-body"><p class="pub-meta"><span>{{ translate("Second author") }}</span></p><p class="pub-description">{{ translate("FAST addresses the cost of analyzing dynamic JavaScript by constructing candidate call paths, then focusing analysis on statements relevant to a potential vulnerability. I implemented JavaScript abstract interpretation and led the evaluation, which found 242 previously unknown vulnerabilities in npm packages.") }}</p><p class="pub-authors">Mingqing Kang, <strong>Yichao Xu</strong>, Song Li, Rigel Gjomemo, Jianwei Hou, V. N. Venkatakrishnan, Yinzhi Cao</p></div></details></article>
<details class="more-items" id="more-publications"><summary><span class="when-closed">{{ translate("Show more") }}</span><span class="when-open">{{ translate("Show less") }}</span><span class="summary-note">{{ translate("3 more papers") }}</span></summary><article class="publication" id="discovery"><details class="work-details"><summary class="work-summary"><span class="entry-label"><span class="entry-marks"><img class="entry-icon" src="assets/icons/journal-text.svg" width="18" height="18" alt="" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="entry-label-text">{{ translate("Preprint 2026") }}</span></span><div class="work-heading"><h3 class="work-title">Discovery or Memorization? A Faithful Benchmark for Real-World Business-Logic Vulnerability Discovery</h3> <span class="work-actions"><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.17542" aria-label="{{ translate('Paper') }}: Discovery or Memorization? A Faithful Benchmark for Real-World Business-Logic Vulnerability Discovery"><img class="link-icon" src="assets/icons/journal-text.svg" width="14" height="14" alt="" aria-hidden="true">{{ translate("Paper") }}</a><a href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2610.17542" aria-label="{{ translate('PDF') }}: Discovery or Memorization? A Faithful Benchmark for Real-World Business-Logic Vulnerability Discovery"><img class="link-icon" src="assets/icons/file-earmark-pdf.svg" width="14" height="14" alt="" aria-hidden="true">PDF</a></span></div></summary><div class="work-body"><p class="pub-meta"><span>{{ translate("arXiv preprint") }}</span></p><p class="pub-description">{{ translate("AnonVul evaluates whether vulnerability-discovery agents find business-logic flaws or rely on recognizable software identity. The benchmark uses anonymized vulnerability tasks, sandboxed execution and expert-defined checks to test discovery performance.") }}</p><p class="pub-authors">Rui Yang, <strong>Yichao Xu</strong>, Zhuohao Zhang, Jiahao Ji, Chaowei Xiao, Yinzhi Cao, Ziyang Li</p></div></details></article>
<article class="publication" id="context"><details class="work-details"><summary class="work-summary"><span class="entry-label"><span class="entry-marks"><img class="entry-icon" src="assets/icons/journal-text.svg" width="18" height="18" alt="" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="entry-label-text">{{ translate("Preprint 2026") }}</span></span><div class="work-heading"><h3 class="work-title">Same Request, Different Boundary: Evaluating Cybersecurity Assistance across Conversational Contexts</h3> <span class="work-actions"><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.00578" aria-label="{{ translate('Paper') }}: Same Request, Different Boundary: Evaluating Cybersecurity Assistance across Conversational Contexts"><img class="link-icon" src="assets/icons/journal-text.svg" width="14" height="14" alt="" aria-hidden="true">{{ translate("Paper") }}</a><a href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2609.00578" aria-label="{{ translate('PDF') }}: Same Request, Different Boundary: Evaluating Cybersecurity Assistance across Conversational Contexts"><img class="link-icon" src="assets/icons/file-earmark-pdf.svg" width="14" height="14" alt="" aria-hidden="true">PDF</a></span></div></summary><div class="work-body"><p class="pub-meta"><span>{{ translate("arXiv preprint") }}</span></p><p class="pub-description">{{ translate("3R-Bench tests how preceding conversation changes an LLM’s response to the same cybersecurity request. It distinguishes refusal, bounded assistance, compliance and provider blocking, separating response behavior from the request itself.") }}</p><p class="pub-authors">Rui Yang, Yang Hong, <strong>Yichao Xu</strong>, Zhengyu Liu, Yinzhi Cao, Ziyang Li</p></div></details></article><article class="publication" id="iot-dos"><details class="work-details"><summary class="work-summary"><span class="entry-label"><span class="entry-marks"><img class="entry-icon" src="assets/icons/journal-text.svg" width="18" height="18" alt="" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="entry-label-text">2018</span></span><h3 class="work-title">A Denial of Services Attack for IOT System</h3></summary><div class="work-body"><p class="pub-meta"><span>{{ translate("Science and Wealth · Jun 2018") }}</span></p><p class="entry-meta">ISSN 1671-2226</p></div></details></article></details></section>
